        "original_id": "70404276-0c12-5f64-90ce-455ed88830d4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Murray Head, Andrew Lloyd Webber, Tim Rice\n- Works: \"Superstar\", Jesus Christ Superstar, \"One Night in Bangkok\", Chess, Say It Ain't So, Find the Crowd\n- Topics: music, acting, live albums\n\nFacts:\n- Murray Head was born on 5 March 1946 and is an English actor and singer.\n- The 1970 rock opera Jesus Christ Superstar was written by Andrew Lloyd Webber and Tim Rice.\n- \"Superstar\" is the title song from the 1970 rock opera Jesus Christ Superstar.\n- Murray Head is most recognized for the song \"Superstar,\" for the 1975 album Say It Ain't So, and for the 1984 single \"One Night in Bangkok\" from the musical Chess.\n- Murray Head's single \"One Night in Bangkok\" topped the charts in various countries.\n- Find the Crowd is a live album by Murray Head recorded at three concerts in France.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
